                <pb facs="0790" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg694"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860c.516/53: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-04-30T12:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 30,
                                1921—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>102. Your 86, April 23, 5 p.m. If American banks subject themselves to
                    regulations of March 23, 1920, will they be permitted legally and actually to
                    join syndicate of paying banks in Poland, or will they be obliged to liquidate
                    completely?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
